It's not actually so bad, once you're at least basic in #riding skill, 
you can pick stuff up from the floor while #riding so it's not often 
that you have to unmount. Except when you want to eat something you 
can't pick up or, as I wanted to, when you want to check that you don't 
#ride over something that will lose you your steed.

Also, when #riding a Dragon, kill purple worms, trappers, lurkers, 
fookatrices, green slime and poisonous monsters from a distance, 
otherwise they might attack your pet instead of you and that would be 
pretty annoying. And don't #ride over chameleon or doppelgaenger 
corpses. Doppelgaengers are actually quite easy to spot, chameleons much 
less so. Sandestines aren't a problem, since they don't leave corpses...

SO, the only thing that you can't guard against 100% is polymorph traps, 
but Gehenomms special layout with respect to where traps will most 
likely be can help you avoid those...

